{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLR9x92spquqphRo6JsJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `sympy.zeros(4, 2).is_upper` now returns `True` instead of raising `IndexError`.\n\n**The fix:** In `sympy/matrices/matrices.py:1115`, the inner loop of `is_upper` now stops at the last column. I changed `for j in range(i)` to `for j in range(min(i, self.cols))`. In a tall matrix, rows below the column count used to make it read entries like `(3, 2)` that don't exist in a 4x2 matrix.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `zeros(4, 2).is_upper` gives `True`.\n- A 4x2 matrix with a non-zero entry below the diagonal correctly gives `False`.\n- `sympy/matrices/tests/test_matrices.py`: 147 passed, 5 failed. The same 5 tests fail without my change: `test_eigen_vects`, `test_issue_3959`, `test_issue_3979`, `test_pinv_rank_deficient` and `test_from_ndarray`.\n\nI didn't add a regression test because the rules for this task don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":19739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"output_tokens":363,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"504d546b-717b-427d-8c95-f1956a2c1213","uuid":"a9d1ee99-2031-4afe-bf15-f62f50eefa68","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:32:27.151Z","request_id":"req_011ChLR9woSURBYC4MS4wHRC"}
